2. LIMITED PERMISSION GRANTED
================================================================================

Subject to the restrictions in section 3, any person obtaining access to the Work
is granted a non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable permission to do the
following, and nothing beyond it:

  * to READ and VIEW the source code and documentation, for the purpose of
    evaluating the Author's technical ability — for example as a recruiter,
    hiring manager, academic admissions reviewer, collaborator, or interviewer;
    and

  * to RUN the Work locally for that purpose — including its test suite and any
    verification, audit or self-check tooling it ships — and to satisfy yourself
    that it does what it claims.

    This second right is deliberate rather than incidental. Several of these
    projects are TOOLS whose documentation invites you to run them, and a licence
    granting only "reading" would have contradicted the README while appearing to
    support it. Anyone auditing a claim made by this Work may execute whatever it
    provides for checking that claim, and may publish what they find — explicitly
    including a refutation. A verification right that excluded publishing a
    negative finding would be worthless.

Running the Work locally to evaluate or check it is therefore permitted. Running
it to provide a service to somebody else is not: see 3.5.

That is the entire grant. No other right is given, by implication, estoppel, or
otherwise.

